+# Authored-Markdown knowledge bundles
+
+## Goal
+Turn authored Markdown documents into a `KnowledgeBundle` so authored content can go
+through the existing bundle import (`read_bundle`/`write_bundle`/`build_snapshot`).
+The result is deterministic: same content, same `bundle_digest`.
+
+## Scope
+Included: new pure domain module `pharma_agent.domain.corpus.authoring` (no I/O, no
+framework imports). Unchanged: `bundle.py`, `models.py`, import, indexing, API, DB.
+
+## Interfaces
+```python
+@dataclass(frozen=True) class AuthoredDocument: key: str; title: str; markdown: str
+    # kind: DocumentKind = GENERAL_MONOGRAPH
+@dataclass(frozen=True) class Section: heading: str; path: tuple[str, ...]; ordinal: int; blocks: list[BlockRecord]
+
+def split_markdown(markdown: str, *, fallback_heading: str) -> list[Section]
+def slugify(text: str, *, max_length: int = 80) -> str
+def section_key(document_key: str, path: Sequence[str]) -> str
+def section_choices(collection: BundleCollection, documents: Sequence[AuthoredDocument]) -> list[tuple[str, str]]
+def build_bundle(collection: BundleCollection, documents: Sequence[AuthoredDocument],
+                 glossary: Sequence[GlossaryEntry], colloquial: Sequence[ColloquialMappingRecord]) -> KnowledgeBundle
+```
+
+## Approach
+- `split_markdown`: line scan tracking fenced code (``` or ~~~ fences; headings inside
+  are ignored). ATX headings `#`..`######` keep a heading stack by level; `path` is the
+  stack including the section's own heading, so the preamble/fallback section (text
+  before the first heading, or a headingless document) has `path == ()` and heading
+  `fallback_heading`. Ordinals are 1-based (as in existing fixtures), counted over kept
+  sections. Sections with no content are dropped.
+- Blocks: within a section, consecutive lines starting with `|` form one table block
+  (`BlockKind.TABLE`, `table_key` `t1`, `t2`, ... numbered across the whole document,
+  including across sections); other text between tables becomes stripped `PROSE` blocks
+  (empty ones skipped). Table lines inside fences are not tables.
+- `slugify`: NFKD, map `đ/Đ` to `d`, drop combining marks, lowercase, ASCII `[a-z0-9]+`
+  words joined by `-`, cut at `max_length` without leaving a trailing hyphen.
+- `section_key` = `<document_key>#` + `/`-joined slugs of path parts, `body` if empty.
+  Slugs that are empty fall back to `section`. Duplicate keys within one document
+  (same heading twice) get `-2`, `-3` suffixes in reading order so the bundle validates.
+- Bundle document key = `f"{collection.key}:{doc.key}"`; section keys are built from it.
+- `section_choices` and `build_bundle` share one internal function producing
+  (bundle document key, section key, section) in order of documents sorted by bundle key.
+  Label = `" › ".join([title, *path])`.
+- `build_bundle`: documents sorted by key; `SourceInfo(title=doc.title)`; one
+  `SectionRecord` per section (`context_path=list(path)`); glossary as given; colloquial
+  mappings keep their records but drop section keys not in the bundle; manifest has
+  collection, generator `pharma-agent-authoring`/`1`, build_id from the content digest,
+  `source_digests` empty, counts, `files={}`. Nothing time- or random-dependent.
+  Duplicate document keys are not checked here; `write_bundle` validation reports them.
+
+## Testing
+`backend/tests/domain/corpus/test_authoring.py`: splitting (fences, preamble, fallback,
+empty sections, paths, ordinals), tables (numbering across sections, prose between),
+slugify/section_key, choices labels, bundle (sorting, prefixing, counts, mapping filter,
+digest determinism, passes `write_bundle`/`read_bundle` round trip and `build_snapshot`).
+Then the full backend suite.
